  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `ContentType=Document` save carrying a valid `document.existingDocumentId`, when the save completes, then EXACTLY ONE `sprk_document` row exists for that document (the pre-existing one) and no second row was created — asserted by a data-mutation integration test that counts rows before and after.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same version save, when it completes, then the SPE drive item's version count is incremented and the drive-item id is UNCHANGED (the same `sprk_graphitemid` the row already carried).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `ContentType=Document` save with NO `document.existingDocumentId`, when the save completes, then a new `sprk_document` is created exactly as it is today — asserted by a contract test that is executing, not skipped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `IsNewVersion` and `VersionComment` on a version save, when the save completes, then neither remains inert: each is either carried into the SPE version call or recorded on the Dataverse row, and the PR states which.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an `existingDocumentId` that does not resolve to a `sprk_document`, when the save is submitted, then it returns a distinct ProblemDetails code (not a generic 500) and creates no row and no SPE item.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an `existingDocumentId` the caller is not authorized on, when the save is submitted, then it is refused by the endpoint filter and no bytes are written to SPE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an existing document row with no SPE pointers, when a version save targets it, then it returns a distinct ProblemDetails code rather than silently falling back to creating a new item.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given `existingDocumentId` sent alongside `ContentType=Email` or `ContentType=Attachment`, when the save runs, then the Email/Attachment behavior is identical to master and the field is not acted on.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git diff` shows no change inside the Email or Attachment branches of `SaveAsync`, and the pre-existing Office tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SaveRequest` gains no `ContainerId` or `FolderPath` member, and the inline warnings at `SaveRequest.cs:24-47` remain intact.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No Microsoft.Graph SDK type appears in `OfficeService.cs`, `OfficeStorageUploader.cs`, or `OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs` after this change (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ContentDedupDetector.cs` is unmodified by this task; verified by `git diff --name-only`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` is green and the full Office contract + integration test set passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size is measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive`, both absolute sizes and the delta are recorded, and the delta is under the +5 MB escalation threshold.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-11 (server half) + Success Criterion 4; plan.md §3 finding F-d and §4 Phase 2 task 023. This task deliberately stops at the server boundary — task 024 sends the field from the client and owns the "Save as new document" override, whose failure mode is NFR-08 data loss. Keep the two halves separable so a rollback of one does not strand the other.
  </notes>

